project/browser-verb-direct-cdp: gm browser verb extension-bridge mode can time out (Extension did not connect). Recover with header session new <name> --direct localhost:9222 (a headless Chrome CDP endpoint is usually already live on :9222/:9223). A header-less body executes JS against the persistent default session (shown in instruction open_browser_sessions browser_sessions[]); it starts on new-tab so navigate inside the body. A body whose first line is session new ONLY creates the session (banner) and does NOT run the JS after it. Witness multi-step flows in ONE header-less body (goto+evaluate).